  "_about": "a ground pangolin SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/new6/pangolin.py): 0.9 m nose to tail tip, the back arched high over the hips, walking low on its hind legs with the forefeet's great claws curled under; a small conical head tapering to a blunt snout; a thick broad tail as long as the body, tapering to its tip; armoured all over the back, flanks, tail and crown in big overlapping scales -- the `pangolin` coat: staggered rows lying back, each with its own shade, a paler free edge and its shadow on the next -- the belly, face and inner limbs bare greyish skin SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw, nail (6 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
